            "en": {
                    "description": "Defender of the Crown combines strategy and action as a Saxon knight captures castles, competes in tournaments and fights for the crown of England. Its spectacular graphics and cinematic presentation made it one of the Amiga's greatest classics.",
                    "history": "In Defender of the Crown, you compete for control of England after the death of King Richard. As a Saxon nobleman, you capture castles, lead armies into battle, enter tournaments and attempt to win the favour of noble ladies. Your ultimate goal is to unite all territories and claim the English crown for yourself.",
                    "review": "Defender of the Crown is one of the greatest classics in computer-game history for me. Its combination of strategy, sieges and tournaments with breathtaking presentation for the period was truly unique. Even on the C64, the game retains a fantastic atmosphere and demonstrates why Cinemaware enjoys legendary status. It is an absolute masterpiece that belongs in every retro collection.",
                    "trivia": [
                        "Developed by Cinemaware and first released for the Amiga in 1986.",
                        "The C64 version is regarded as one of the most technically impressive conversions of its time.",
                        "Defender of the Crown helped establish Cinemaware's reputation."
                    ],
                    "worthPlaying": "Defender of the Crown remains captivating through its unique mixture of strategy, action and cinematic presentation. Despite its age, it possesses a special charm and is one of those games every retro enthusiast should experience at least once."
                }
