            "en": {
                    "description": "Sid Meier combines trading, naval battles and exploration in one of the best-known strategy games of the 1980s.",
                    "history": "In Sid Meier's Pirates!, you take on the role of a privateer in the seventeenth-century Caribbean. You sail between the colonies of the European powers, trade goods, fight enemy ships, search for hidden treasure and hunt notorious pirates. Your choices determine whether history remembers you as a feared pirate or a respected privateer.",
                    "review": "Sid Meier's Pirates! is one of the most timeless classics ever made for me. Its ideal combination of naval battles, trading, treasure hunting and exploration still provides countless hours of enjoyment today. Hardly any other game captures the feeling of being a pirate as convincingly as this masterpiece. Pirates! remains one of the finest games ever developed and is an absolute highlight of video-game history, whether played on the C64 or the Amiga.",
                    "trivia": [
                        "Designed by legendary game designer Sid Meier.",
                        "Combines action, strategy, trading and role-playing elements in a single game.",
                        "The game received a remake in 2004."
                    ],
                    "worthPlaying": "Sid Meier's Pirates! remains compelling thanks to its remarkable freedom of play. Every voyage unfolds differently and offers an excellent mixture of naval combat, exploration, trading and pirate adventure. This variety makes it a timeless classic even decades after its original release."
                }
