                    "description": "Doom is id Software's classic first-person shooter, which transformed PC gaming in 1993 through fast action, network play, shareware distribution and exceptional support for modification.",
                    "history": "Doom was released for DOS in December 1993. id Software initially distributed its first episode as shareware, while the registered full version could be ordered directly. This mail-order model is an important part of Doom's early history and explains this entry's particular packaging. Technically, Doom established new standards in speed, level presentation and multiplayer. Its openly documented data structure also made it easier to create custom levels and modifications.",
                    "review": "Doom still needs almost no preparation. Within seconds, it becomes clear why the game was so influential. Movement, weapons and enemies interact with an immediacy that many modern shooters deliberately imitate. The original controls benefit from sensible modern configuration, but otherwise Doom has aged remarkably little. A mail-order box also makes it a fascinating piece of distribution history.",
