                    "history": "Heretic was developed by Raven Software and published by id Software in 1994. It uses an enhanced Doom engine but adds fantasy weapons, an inventory and new viewing and movement features. The full version originally sold directly and by mail order contained three episodes. A later expanded edition, Shadow of the Serpent Riders, added further episodes.",
                    "review": "Heretic is far more than Doom with magic wands. Its level design, weapons and especially its inventory create a pace of their own. Some areas now feel labyrinthine, but clear controls and rapid combat remain remarkably effective. The mail-order box is also an attractive collectible from the era of direct PC-game distribution.",
