                    "description": "Tass Times in Tonetown is an eccentric 1986 adventure that combines typed commands with graphical controls and sends players into a bizarre new-wave parallel dimension.",
                    "history": "Tass Times in Tonetown was released in 1986 for several home computers and as a PC booter. It was developed by Interplay and Brainwave Creations and published by Activision. The story concerns a grandfather whose dream machine creates an alternate reality. Players travel to Tonetown, a deliberately bizarre world filled with new-wave fashion, unusual slang and talking characters.",
