                    "history": "Released in 1994, the game was developed by Beavis Soft and distributed by Apogee. Like many Apogee titles, Wacky Wheels used the shareware model: part of the game could be tried freely before ordering the full version directly. This mail-order edition is therefore particularly interesting as a physical collectible.",
                    "review": "Wacky Wheels is pleasantly direct. Rather than complex driving physics, it offers fast arcade races, obstacles and attacks against rivals. Its age is technically apparent, but the multiplayer appeal and clear design still work.",
